<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agilolfings</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 555–788</span> · Also known as Agilolfing dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Agilolfings were a noble family that ruled the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> from about 555 to 788 and also provided kings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a>. Recognised by the Frankish kings from Garibald I onwards, the dukes governed almost as kings, issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lex-baiuvariorum">Lex Baiuvariorum</a> and founded bishoprics and monasteries. The last duke, Tassilo III, was deposed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> in 788.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agilolfings.jpg" alt="Agilolfings" width="320" height="528" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fratelli Zavattari · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Theodelinda_married_Agilulf_(detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
